}
```

**Choices made:**
- **Compat entry points, not the main `es-toolkit` exports.** The main `startCase` lowercases word tails, so `HTML` becomes `Html`, which differs from lodash. The main `merge` replaces arrays instead of merging them index by index, which also differs. The compat versions match lodash. `truncate` is only available from compat anyway.
- **No adapters.** The call shapes already match, so none are needed. No replacement logic was hand-written, and no lodash import remains.
- **Subpath imports** (`es-toolkit/compat/merge` and so on) keep the bundle small by pulling in only what each function needs.

